+| `Rule30ZeroWallDiagonals` | 2026-11-10 | Left diagonals of the zero-boundary left half, measured from the moving edge of a nonzero finite row (`E L m j t = zrow L t (m + t - j)`), obey the left-diagonal recurrence whenever the entry guard `j + 2 ≤ m + t` holds, equality included (`E_entry`, `E_tailLeft`). For every array with eventually black coordinates 0 and 1 and such an eventual recurrence (`TailLeft`), each coordinate has eventual period `2 ^ j` (`tail_periodic`), `Q`-periodic profiles obey `M + 3 ≤ 2 ^ (2 Q)` (`tail_profile_bound`), and eventually white and eventually black coordinates both occur at arbitrarily large index (`tail_white_unbounded`, `tail_no_two_white`, `tail_black_after_white`, `tail_black_unbounded`, `E_black_unbounded`). Hence the free word of a finitely supported constrained row has bounded lag for bounded-slack repeats (`freeWord_bounded_lag`, `freeWord_bounded_lag_of_finSupp`), and, with the binary special-factor count (`factorCount_succ`, known) and an explicit two-run witness (`two_run`), its factor complexity exceeds `n + K` eventually for every `K` (`complexity_of_bounded_lag`, `freeWord_complexity`). Such rows exist only if `Q01` fails; the free-word statements are conditional. Contributed by Gareth Herbert with Claude (Anthropic) and GPT (OpenAI), as Rule 30 Prize submission [PORTAL-ID](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/PORTAL-ID). | `E_entry`, `E_tailLeft`, `tail_periodic`, `tail_profile_bound`, `tail_white_unbounded`, `tail_no_two_white`, `tail_black_after_white`, `tail_black_unbounded`, `E_black_unbounded`, `row_eq_Theta`, `rows_agree`, `freeWord_bounded_lag`, `freeWord_bounded_lag_of_finSupp`, `le_factorCount`, `factorCount_le`, `factorCount_succ`, `rightSpecialCount_pos`, `two_run`, `complexity_of_bounded_lag`, `freeWord_complexity` |
